# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# lychee link-checker ignore list
#
# Patterns are PCRE2 regex matched against the full URL/file path. Lines
# starting with '#' are comments. Be conservative — every entry here is a
# real broken link we're choosing not to enforce.
#
# Categories below mark what kind of exception each block represents.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ─── Category 1: Content not yet authored ────────────────────────────────────
# These paths are referenced from concept stubs, learning-path overviews, and
# the root README as forward references to content we'll write next. They'll
# resolve to real files as the curriculum lands. When a path here is filled
# in, remove the matching line so the checker re-enforces it.

# Concept pages (forward references from learning paths and the root README)
# Note: concepts/agents/{what-is-an-agent,agent-loop,react-pattern,agents-vs-frameworks}.md authored.
# Note: concepts/tools/{tool-design,tool-selection,search-tools}.md authored (batches 7, 9).
# Note: concepts/rag/{what-is-rag,retrieval-as-a-tool,chunking-and-indexing}.md authored (batch 10).
# Note: concepts/rag/{retrieval-strategies,hybrid-search,reranking}.md authored (batch 11).
# Note: concepts/rag/{contextual-retrieval,query-rewriting,retrieval-failure-modes}.md authored (batch 12).
# Note: concepts/evaluation/{what-is-rag-evaluation,eval-set-construction,retrieval-metrics,answer-quality-metrics}.md authored (batch 13).
^.*/concepts/agents/plan-and-execute\.md$
^.*/concepts/context/context-budget\.md$

# Pattern pages (referenced from concept pages but not yet authored)
^.*/patterns/01-single-agent-tool-use\.md$
^.*/patterns/03-supervisor-workers\.md$
^.*/patterns/06-plan-and-execute\.md$
^.*/patterns/10-human-in-the-loop\.md$

# Math pages not yet authored
